<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amalie Zephyrine of Salm-Kyrburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1760">1760</a>–<a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amalie Zephyrine of Salm-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrburg">Kyrburg</a> was the wife of Prince Anton Aloys of Hohenzollern-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen">Sigmaringen</a>. Living apart from her husband in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, she befriended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephine-de-beauharnais">Joséphine de Beauharnais</a>, and her influence with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s circle helped Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen survive the mediatisation of 1806 as a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a>. Her brother, Prince Frederick III of Salm-Kyrburg, was guillotined in 1794.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amalie-zephyrine-of-salm-kyrburg.jpg" alt="Amalie Zephyrine of Salm-Kyrburg" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste François Laby (1784–1860) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laby_-_Amalie_Zephyrine_von_Salm-Kyrburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
